     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I am trying to make the first label of my radio button choices bold.<div>I can get the first label (and not the rest) of the radiobutton to be bold using this code:</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"color:#000\">   tags$style</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">HTML</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;.radio label:first-child{font-weight:bold&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><div><br><div>However, this makes the first label of all radiobutton groups bold. I have several radiobutton groups and I only want one of the groups to be bold.</div><div>When I specify between groups using class and modify the above code to the class name (.rbutton1 instead of .radio) and use this line of code:</div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">  tags$style</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">HTML</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;.rbutton1 .radio label:first-child{font-weight:bold&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div>only labels from the specified radio button grouping are bold but all labels, not just the first label, are bold. In the example below, I want only &quot;Zero&quot; to be bold.<br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>ui.R<div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><